	abstract = {We show global well-posedness of the dynamic \${\textbackslash}Phi{\textasciicircum}4\_3\$ model on the torus. This model is given by a non-linear stochastic PDE that can only be interpreted in a renormalised sense. A local well-posedness theory for this equation was recently developed by Hairer as well as Gubininell, Perkowski, Imkeller and Catellier, Chouk. In the present article, we show that these solutions cannot blow up in finite time. Our method relies entirely on deterministic PDE arguments (such as embeddings of Besov spaces and interpolation), which are combined to derive energy inequalities.},
